    Option D - Archive old logs (move and compress)
    
    I created /workspace/archive-logs.sh which moves files older than RETENTION_DAYS from LOG_DIR to ARCHIVE_DIR and optionally compresses them. Defaults: 
logdir=/var/logs, archive-dir=/var/log_archive, retention=7 days, archive-retention=90 days.
    
    Install:
    
       sudo cp /workspace/archive-logs.sh /usr/local/bin/archive-logs.sh
       sudo chmod 755 /usr/local/bin/archive-logs.sh
    
    Cron example (hourly):
    
       sudo bash -c 'cat > /etc/cron.d/archive-logs <<EOF
    0 * * * * root /usr/local/bin/archive-logs.sh --logdir /var/logs --retention 7 --archive-dir /var/log_archive >> /var/log/archive-logs-cron.log 2>&1
    EOF'
    
    Test:
    
       /workspace/archive-logs.sh --logdir /tmp/testlogs --retention 0 --archive-dir /tmp/testarchive --dry-run
    
    Caution: ensure the archive partition has sufficient space. For remote archival, consider rsync/scp to remote storage and rotate/prune archives as 
needed.
    

